{number: 130}
{title: Blessed Be The Fountain}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Blessed be the fountain of blood,
To a [F] world of [C] sinners re-[G7] vealed;
[C] Blessed be the dear Son of God:
Only [F] by His [G7] stripes we are [C] healed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
The [C] blood of Jesus cleanseth and washes as [F] white as the [C] snow;
Blessed be the [G7] fountain of blood,
Only [F] by His [G7] stripes we are [C] healed.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Though my sins were as scarlet,
He [F] washed them as [C] white as the [G7] snow;
[C] Blessed be the dear Son of God:
From His [F] side the [G7] healing streams [C] flow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Sing the praise of Jesus our King,
To the [F] ends of the [C] earth be it [G7] told;
[C] Blessed be the fountain of blood,
More [F] precious than [G7] silver and [C] gold.
{end_of_verse}
